WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.150
In Venezuela, cars don’t depreciate.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.340
You could buy one today, drive it for five
or six years, and then sell it for the same

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:11.940
price you paid.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.210
And you can forget about gas.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:22.230
At just over six cents a gallon, you can fill
up your tank for less than one U.S. Dollar.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:27.260
In Venezuela, banks offer loans for plastic
surgery.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.720
Taxi drivers earn higher salaries than doctors.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.880
Supermarkets are equipped with fingerprint
scanners.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:41.870
And some find it cheaper to live year-round
in luxury hotels than rent an apartment.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.090
Sponsored by Brilliant.

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:50.840
